    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d252">

                <pb facs="0230" n="156" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg156"/>

                <head>Sir F. Bruce to Mr. Hunter</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 18, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to transmit to you copies
                    of a despatch, and of its enclosures, which I have received from her Majesty’s
                    consul at Boston, relative to a tax of thirty cents a ton which is being levied
                    upon British vessels at the ports within his consulate, the measurement being,
                    as it appears, taken under the old system, whereby the British register tonnage
                    is increased nearly one-third.</p>
                <p>I beg that you will have the goodness to submit these documents to the proper
                    authorities, and I trust that, in accordance with the suggestion of her
                    Majesty’s consul, the additional tax which appears to have been unduly levied
                    upon British vessels since the 1st April may be remitted, and that, in future,
                    the tax in question will be assessed upon the tonnage borne upon the registers
                    of the British vessels.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, sir, your most obedient humble
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FREDERICK W. A. BRUCE.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Hunter,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>






